templates.description:
H3C Comware V7 production-candidate SNMP template for Zabbix 7.0 LTS.

Baseline: H3C Comware Production by SNMP 2.0.0-rc1.6.
Scope: Comware V7. Private-MIB implementation remains product/model dependent and must be validated on representative devices.

rc2.0-v7:
- CPU/memory thresholds remain 80/90%; interface utilization remains 80/90%.
- Sustained interface error threshold 5 pps; burst 500 pps.
- Sustained interface discard threshold 10 pps; burst 1000 pps.
- Link-flap threshold 8 changes/10m.
- MSTP root-change alert disabled by default.
- All IRF alarms require {$IRF.ALERT}=1; default disabled.
- Optical DDM alarms remain disabled by default and additionally require DDM=supported.
- Interface speed-decrease change event disabled by default.
- Half-duplex alarm is macro-controlled.
- Removed the deprecated no-effect physical-interface-type compatibility macro.

Before broad rollout, validate MIB support, returned values, indexes and trigger behavior on representative Comware V7 models.
rc2.1 community-template audit:
- current HH3C community template 7.4-2 was reviewed;
- ICMP loss, system/ENTITY inventory, interface discards, ifType and duplex were already present and retained;
- system/firmware/serial/OS change events are disabled by default via {$SYSTEM.CHANGE.ALERT};
- optional SNMP trap fallback remains disabled;
- fixed-index calculated summary items and more-sensitive ICMP/temperature defaults were not imported.

rc2.2 UUID correction:
- template and all child-object UUID fields regenerated as RFC 4122 UUIDv4;
- template-group UUID retained from the source export;
- monitoring logic unchanged from rc2.1.


rc2.3 module-discovery accuracy correction:
- reviewed an additional Zabbix 5.4 H3C Switch General Template;
- adopted its useful ENTITY-MIB entPhysicalClass=module(9) constraint;
- retained the stricter existing Module Level1/Fabric Module description filter;
- did not import its legacy SNMP availability, text uptime, CPU/memory trigger thresholds, interface trigger logic, SNMP community macro or unused threshold macros.
- monitoring thresholds and alert policy are otherwise unchanged from rc2.2.

temperature validity correction:
- hh3cEntityExtTemperature now discards absurd/out-of-range values before trigger evaluation;
- this specifically prevents the H3C documented invalid value 65535 from becoming a false high-temperature alert;
- normal warning/critical temperature thresholds are unchanged.


rc2.4 recovery-expression import correction:
- removed invalid macro-only recovery expressions from system/firmware/serial/OS change-event triggers;
- these change events now use Zabbix default expression-based recovery;
- {$SYSTEM.CHANGE.ALERT}=1 remains in the problem expression;
- no OID, threshold, polling interval or other alert policy was changed.


rc3.1 / Zabbix 7.0 LTS / Comware V7:
- independent V7 template identity; designed to coexist with the V5 template;
- do not use host-level Replace against hosts that still contain entities preserved from the legacy template;
- use directly on V7 hosts/new V7 onboarding.


rc3.2 graph-name isolation (H3C V7):
- all LLD graph prototype names are namespaced by Comware major version;
- this intentionally prevents Zabbix host-side uniqueness collisions with legacy/orphan discovered graphs that have the same name but a different item set;
- graph UUIDs, item prototype UUIDs, item keys, OIDs, thresholds and history-bearing items are unchanged from rc3.1;
- dashboard graph-prototype references were updated to the new names.

